WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:04.026
- The disproportional reason so
many people in here will not

00:00:04.026 --> 00:00:08.530
win, let's just get right to
the chase, the disproportionate

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.701
reason that most people in this
room will not win is actually

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:15.370
not the hard work which is what
I'm gonna talk about probably

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.473
for next 45 minutes.

00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:21.577
It's your lack of patience.

00:00:21.577 --> 00:00:25.196
(applause)

00:00:25.196 --> 00:00:27.750
For some unknown
reason when people go into

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.587
ventures like this and other
things they somehow miraculously

00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:34.223
think it's going to
happen in five minutes.

00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:37.359
That you're the one person in
the world, whatever you guys

00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:41.230
call your big club and put
posters of each other up on you

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:44.700
think you're going to be in that
circle in five minutes for some

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.536
reason 'cause you're the most
charismatic, you figured out

00:00:47.536 --> 00:00:51.640
some weird system, 
you've got it.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.973
And the lack of patience is 
what hurts so many people.

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:59.330
From 22 to 30 years old 
for eight years in my

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.899
20s I worked 15 hours a day,

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:04.335
seven days a week in my
dad's liquor store.

00:01:04.335 --> 00:01:08.065
Today, with all things that have
happened to me, I get emails on

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:11.135
Facebook from friends I went to
high school with often starting

00:01:11.135 --> 00:01:13.137
with, "Gary, you're so lucky."

00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:15.573
I reply to every
single one of them.

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:18.943
All of them with the reply
of an opening line first,

00:01:18.943 --> 00:01:21.279
"Jan, great to see you again.
You look great.

00:01:21.279 --> 00:01:22.213
"Kid's super cute.

00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:25.216
"P.S. I am super not lucky.

00:01:25.216 --> 00:01:29.186
"Let me remind you, Rick,
remember when we graduated

00:01:29.186 --> 00:01:32.690
"college and you went to the
Jersey Shore every weekend and

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.458
"hooked up with
chicks and drank beer.

00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:35.760
"I worked."

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.379
(upbeat music)

